# Storybook copy source

**Show code is off by default** (`.storybook/preview.tsx` + `storyMetaDocsDefaults()`). Only **Pattern** stories opt in.

## When to show code

| Story kind | Show code? | How |
|------------|------------|-----|
| **Pattern — …** | Yes | **`storyCopySource()`** or **`withStoryCopySource()`** |
| **Anatomy** | No | Rely on default — specimen + slot tables |
| **Reference — …** | No | Rely on default — visual gallery |
| **Usage / Best practices** (meta `docs.description.component`) | No | Markdown only — never a story canvas |

## Snippet rules (Pattern stories only)

- **Include imports** — `@whatmatters/wmds`, `lucide-react`, `useState` when needed.
- **JSX the app pastes** — inside a component `return`, or a small named wrapper when stateful.
- **No CSF** — never `name`, `parameters`, `render`, `export const …`.
- **No demo chrome** — no `max-w-md`, `p-4`, specimen borders in the snippet (keep in `render`).

Helpers: **`src/lib/storyCopySource.ts`**.

## Before merge

1. **Pattern** story → **Show code** visible with drop-in snippet.
2. **Anatomy / Reference** → no **Show code** block.
3. If CSF or story `render` leaks into docs, fix — you forgot **`storyCopySource()`** or the global default was overridden.

See **`AGENTS.md` → Storybook copy source**.
